# CAR with PV1_0 = 1 and only PV1_1 given (phi_0 = 10), no PV1_2
# (synthetic, hand-written). wcslib 8.10 celset passes (phi_0, theta_0)
# to the projection only with PV1_0 = 1, and prjoff then computes the
# offset (x_0, y_0) = the projection of (phi_0, theta_0) only when BOTH are
# defined; with PV1_2 missing it sets the projection's own default
# fiducial point and NO offset, while the given PV1_1 still enters
# celset's native-to-celestial rotation. A reader that applies the offset
# whenever PV1_0 = 1 is 10-20 px off here.
NOTE pipeline: CAR with PV1_0 = 1 and only PV1_1 (offset not applied)
GRID 1.13 498.71 15 1.29 498.53 15
SKYGRID 0.71 359.13 13 -89.37 89.21 13
